entry.summary:
Coding vs Programming (A Beginner’s Realization) A few days ago, I was sitting in our institute and talking with my friend Bala. “Hey… what’s the difference between coding and programming?” I opened web and YT. The Moment Something Clicked While searching, I found a video explaining the difference between coding and programming. At first, I expected some complicated technical explanation. Coding = Programming Same thing. Different words. Coding is the part most beginners see first. if(password === userInput){ console.log("Login successful") }
This is coding. Programming is something deeper. If the password is correct → allow login
That is not syntax. After watching the explanation, I started thinking about a simple analogy. Recently, I decided to start doing something different in my learning journey. Before Bala asked that question, my learning mindset was simple That conversation with Bala made me realize something important. That small conversation with Bala didn’t just teach me the difference between coding and programming. Starting tomorrow. 🚀
